This profile uses real threads, native file/directory capabilities, monotonic
time and byte-pipe stdio. It provides no Linux process identity, dynamic loader,
CPU-time substitute, TCP transport, subprocess, watcher or formatter. Upstream
Lua configuration, plugins, client configuration editing and custom annotations
use the existing filesystem authority. Lazy-cache paths use owned instance
state. No launcher/network/SDK grant is requested. Inherited filesystem authority may
include writable home; instance names are not a confidentiality boundary.

